content.text:
Here is the complete, ordered picture of what happens when an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`.

## Overview of the call chain

`POST /api/owners` → `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)` (implements the generated `OwnersApi.addOwner`) → a sequence of inline normalizers/validators → `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner(...)` → `OwnerRepository.save(...)` (JPA impl) → `Owner`'s `@PrePersist`. On success `OwnerAuditor.ownerCreated(...)` logs an audit entry. Exceptions are translated by `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.

---

## 1. The mapping and the controller method

### Route definition (generated interface)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java`

- Interface is annotated `@Validated` (line 44), `@Tag(...)` (line 45).
- Path constant `PATH_ADD_OWNER = "/owners"` (line 52).
- The `addOwner` default method is mapped (lines 79-86):
```java
@RequestMapping(
    method = RequestMethod.POST,
    value = OwnersApi.PATH_ADD_OWNER,          // "/owners"
    produces = { "application/json" },
    consumes = { "application/json" }
)
default ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(
    @Parameter(name = "OwnerFieldsDto", description = "The pet owner", required = true) @Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto
)
```
So the effective route is `/api` (class-level `@RequestMapping("/api")`) + `/owners` = **POST /api/owners**. The request body is `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, meaning Bean Validation on the DTO runs before the controller body executes.

### Controller implementation
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

Class annotations (lines 68-71): `@RestController`, `@CrossOrigin(exposedHeaders = "errors, content-type")`, `@RequestMapping("/api")`, `implements OwnersApi`.

Constants (lines 77-90): `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50`, `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100`, `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80`.

The handler (lines 139-183):
```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    ownerFieldsDto.setAddress(AddressNormalizer.normalize(ownerFieldsDto.getAddress()));
    List<String> missingFields = OwnerFieldsValidator.findMissingFields(ownerFieldsDto);
    if (!missingFields.isEmpty()) {
        throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missingFields);
    }
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    if (!PostcodeValidator.isValidForCity(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode())) {
        throw new InvalidPostcodeException(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity());
    }
    if (this.clinicService.countOwnersByCity(owner.getCity()) >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY) {
        throw new CityCapacityExceededException(owner.getCity());
    }
    if (RegistrationDatePolicy.isAfterServerDate(owner.getRegistrationDate())) {
        throw new FutureRegistrationDateException(owner.getRegistrationDate());
    }
    LocalDate registrationDate = RegistrationDatePolicy.effectiveDate(owner.getRegistrationDate());
    if (this.clinicService.countOwnersRegisteredOn(registrationDate) >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY) {
        throw new DailyOwnerLimitExceededException(registrationDate);
    }
    owner.setTelephone(TelephoneNormalizer.normalize(owner.getTelephone()));
    owner.setEmail(EmailNormalizer.normalize(owner.getEmail()));
    if (DisposableEmailValidator.isDisposable(owner.getEmail())) {
        throw new DisposableEmailException(owner.getEmail());
    }
    owner.setHouseholdId(HouseholdIdGenerator.generate(owner.getLastName(), owner.getPostcode()));
    boolean declaredHouseholdMember = Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold());
    owner.setDeclaredHouseholdMember(declaredHouseholdMember);
    if (!declaredHouseholdMember && this.clinicService.isHouseholdDuplicate(owner)) {
        throw new DuplicateIdentityException(owner.getIdentityKey());
    }
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    this.ownerAuditor.ownerCreated(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = toOwnerDtoWithBulkSignupWarning(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

Note the controller method itself has **no `@Transactional`** (only `deleteOwner` in this class does, line 216). Each `clinicService.*` call is its own transaction.

Helper it uses (lines 190-196), which does an extra count query on every create/read response:
```java
private OwnerDto toOwnerDtoWithBulkSignupWarning(Owner owner) {
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    LocalDate today = RegistrationDatePolicy.effectiveDate(null);
    ownerDto.setBulkSignupWarning(
        this.clinicService.countOwnersRegisteredOn(today) > BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD);
    return ownerDto;
}
```

There is also a V2 controller (`OwnerRestControllerV2.java`) but it only exposes `GET` paging (`listOwnersPage`); it has no create path.

---

## 2. Request DTO and Bean Validation annotations

`/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/dto/OwnerFieldsDto.java` (generated from the OpenAPI spec). Validation constraints are on the getters:

- `firstName` (line 76): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `lastName` (line 97): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `address` (line 118): `@NotNull @Size(min = 1, max = 255)`
- `city` (line 139): `@NotNull @Size(min = 1, max = 80)`
- `postcode` (line 160, optional): `@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{4}$")`
- `telephone` (line 181): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9()+\\-.\\s]*$") @Size(min = 1, max = 20)`
- `email` (line 202, optional): `@Size(max = 255) @jakarta.validation.constraints.Email`
- `birthDate` (line 223, optional): `@Valid` (LocalDate)
- `registrationDate` (line 244, optional): `@Valid` (LocalDate)
- `sharesHousehold` (line 268, optional): no constraint, defaults to `false` (line 50)

These fire first because of `@Valid @RequestBody`; a violation throws `MethodArgumentNotValidException` (handled in the advice, see section 7).

The `Owner` **entity** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`) is a separate class the DTO is mapped into. Its own Bean Validation / JPA annotations (lines 38-93):
- Class: `@Entity @Table(name = "owners")`, extends `Person`.
- `address` (line 41-43): `@Column @NotEmpty`
- `city` (line 45-47): `@Column @NotEmpty`
- `postcode` (line 49-50): `@Column`
- `telephone` (line 52-55): `@Column @NotEmpty @Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", message = "Phone number must be in E.164 form")`
- `email` (line 57-58): `@Column`
- plus `birthDate`, `registrationDate`, `customerCode`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, `householdSize`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, a `@Transient declaredHouseholdMember` (lines 89-90), and `@OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL, mappedBy = "owner", fetch = FetchType.EAGER) Set<Pet> pets` (line 92-93).

Parent `Person` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`, lines 28-37): `@MappedSuperclass`, `firstName` and `lastName` both `@Column @NotEmpty`.

Base `BaseEntity` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/BaseEntity.java`): `@Id @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY) Integer id`; `isNew()` returns `id == null` (lines 33-47). This drives insert-vs-update decisions.

The DTO→entity mapping is MapStruct (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`, lines 48-50): `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores `id` and `pets`.

---

## 3. Custom validators / @InitBinder / Validator classes

There are **no** `@InitBinder` methods, no `WebDataBinder` configuration, and **no** classes implementing Spring's `Validator` interface anywhere in `src/main` (searched). All "validation" in the create path is either declarative Bean Validation on the DTO (section 2) or the plain static helper classes invoked imperatively in the controller:

