**JPA lifecycle callback on `Owner`** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (lines 101-104):
```java
@PrePersist
private void resolveRegistrationDate() {
    this.registrationDate = RegistrationDatePolicy.effectiveDate(this.registrationDate);
}
```
This runs at `em.persist` time and defaults/weekend-adjusts the registration date once more. This is the **only** lifecycle callback (`@PrePersist`) in the model — there are no `@PostPersist/@PreUpdate/@PostLoad` anywhere. `Owner.pets` cascades `ALL`, but on create the set is empty (mapper ignores `pets`), so nothing cascades.

