## 6. Security / authorization annotations

- Controller handler: `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` on `addOwner` (line 139) and on every other method in `OwnerRestControllerV1`.
- No `@PreAuthorize` on the service layer.
- Method security enabled by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/BasicAuthenticationConfig.java`: `@Configuration @EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled = true) @ConditionalOnProperty(name = "petclinic.security.enable", havingValue = "true")` (lines 18-21). Filter chain (lines 33-43) disables CSRF, requires auth on all requests, uses HTTP Basic; JDBC-backed users/roles (lines 45-54). **Security is only active when `petclinic.security.enable=true`.**
- The `@roles` SpEL bean is `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/Roles.java` (`@Component`): `OWNER_ADMIN = "ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN"` (line 8).

